; The pounce, with its guard. Winning 42 pp. 43-46 (S-0064-a, S-0064-b,
; S-0064-e, S-0064-f, S-0066-e, S-0067-b) and p. 55 (S-0079-b, S-0079-c);
; played in Hands 28, 29, 30 and 32 (S-0130-e, S-0133-b, S-0136-a, S-0142-l),
; and lost in Hand 15 (S-0049-b); its companion's play in Hand 35 trick 1, the
; 4-2 kept the 4-1 back on the bidder's top trump (S-0150-e, no reason given).
; Rule, in our words: a setter puts count only on a trick his side may take.
; Playing before his partner to a lead from the bidder's side that his partner
; may still beat, he plays count at once, a ten before a five, whether or not
; he can follow (p. 46: play it or lose it). If he holds the double of the
; suit led and count outside his hand may still fall, he plays the double
; instead (p. 44); but a double cannot win count he holds himself, so then he
; plays the count (Hand 28 trick 3). Once his partner has played and the trick
; is the other side's beyond his reach, he plays no count.
; Reading: the trick his partner may still beat is one the led suit can lose:
; a live tile outside his hand follows it and beats the tile taking it, and
; his partner has not shown void there. His partner's possible ruff does not
; count. A double, or a tile the top of its suit, is as good as a double and
; no trick to pounce on (S-0079-b), and in Hands 30 and 31 (trick 2 and 3) the
; setter throws a plain tile on the bidder's partner's 0-0 though his own
; partner had not shown out of trump (S-0135-f, S-0139-d).
; Replaces gates/c07-pounce.silas. How it differs: the gate fires whenever the
; seat after the bidder cannot follow, including a lead nothing can beat (the
; top trump, a walker, S-0066-e and S-0079-b); the book's premise is a trick
; the setters may take. The gate needs a void; the book pounces while able to
; follow (Hands 28 and 30, trick 3). The gate has no rule for the seat after
; the partner (S-0064-f, S-0079-c) and no double (S-0064-e). The book's "more
; urgent against 35 and 36" (S-0143-d) ranks the rule; it changes no tile.
; Hand 30 trick 3 is the rule's DD-visible failure (S-0136-a); it is still the
; book's play.

(include book)

(policy pounce
  (rule no-count-on-a-lost-trick (play give)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (partner me pard)
    (some (roles his) (trick-play pard his))
    (current-winner w)
    (opponent me w)
    (trick-play w win)
    (led-context q)
    (none (roles over) (own-legal over) (beats over win q))
    (own-legal give)
    (count give 0)
    (own-legal held)
    (count-tile held))
  (rule win-with-the-double (play dd)
    (roles me pard l led dd q)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (partner me pard)
    (none (roles his) (trick-play pard his))
    (leader l)
    (opponent me l)
    (trick-play l led)
    (led-context q)
    (own-legal dd)
    (double dd)
    (in dd q)
    (beats dd led q)
    (calls-for-count led))
  (rule play-a-ten-now (play give)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (leader l)
    (opponent me l)
    (partner-may-take-it)
    (own-legal give)
    (count give 10))
  (rule play-a-five-now (play give)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (leader l)
    (opponent me l)
    (partner-may-take-it)
    (own-legal give)
    (count give 5)))
